# Vauxhall Viva HB two-door saloon, 1966-1970.
#
# The HB Viva: the longer, wider replacement for the HA, with the 1,159 cc
# and 1,975 cc engines and the coke-bottle styling, sold from September 1966.
# The two-door saloon is modelled; the four-door, the estate and the GT are
# not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Viva
#
# Dimensions 4.105 x 1.600 x 1.354 m, wheelbase 2.432 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is near-level, about 8-10 degrees forward, so the
# flank is a close estimate and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Green are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 145 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro September 1966; retires staggered 1979-1982 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-hb.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-hb.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-viva-hb/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the two-door saloon is modelled with the rectangular
# headlamps of the front reference; the four-door body photographed there is
# not copied, only its nose. The near-side trace is perspective-corrected
# approximately.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallVivaHB(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1966
intro_month=9
retire_year=1982
retire_month=6
speed=145
